en had  cheated but they told him never to do it  again that it wasn't okay what the  report calls a quote clear stand against  cheating end quote and apparently borup  and tessus were never told about this  situation and management was seemingly  never informed when we told him  that this box should under no  circumstances be used in the game again  we trusted that he would not do so  and that's also why it was not  communicated to borob and tessa's that  the buck had been used which looking  back at it we should have and we should  probably have the team meeting and said  what what the [ __ ] is going on here i  think we can all agree that it was a  huge mistake for the players not to make  the others aware but for esik at least  hunden failed to prove that the players  minus nico were complicit in his  cheating scheme in any way the report  also confirmed something else alleged by  hunden to tv2 and then discussed at  length in the counter-strike community  which was the fact that heroic tried to  have its players sign an nda or  non-disclosure agreement about this  whole situation but if the organization  attempted to have the players sign this  nda and it would prevent discussion of  this entire incident  why have they not faced any consequences  the esic report says that because of big  changes to both management and ownership  at heroic since the coaching bug scandal  quote it is important to distinguish  this statement's indication of failings  and poor decisions by the previous  management administering the  organization at the time of the  spectator bug scandal from the current  ownership and management team the nda  was also seemingly a reaction to the  august 2020 ban and not to some  revelations of cheating surfacing after  the astralis match where it was first  used by hunden which the report says  they didn't hear about the nda is  painted as a misguided pr effort and not  a total cover-up attempt in the report  in heroic's response video cadian says 